</description><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Peter Florijn</dc:creator><pubDate>Fri, 01 Mar 2024 15:35:00 +0100</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="false">tag:blog.florijnconsultancy.nl,2024-03-01:/articles/Hurt - Johnny Cash.html</guid><category>Music</category><category>chordify</category></item><item><title>Wicked game - Chris Isaak</title><link>https://blog.florijnconsultancy.nl/articles/Wicked%20game%20-%20Chris%20Isaak.html</link><description>&lt;iframe frameborder="0" height="500" src="https://chordify.net/embed/chris-isaak-songs/wicked-game-3-chords" width="100%"&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;</description><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Peter Florijn</dc:creator><pubDate>Wed, 28 Feb 2024 10:44:00 +0100</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="false">tag:blog.florijnconsultancy.nl,2024-02-28:/articles/Wicked game - Chris Isaak.html</guid><category>Music</category><category>chordify</category><category>chords</category><category>guitar</category></item><item><title>Recording in Ableton with MOTU M2 loopback</title><link>https://blog.florijnconsultancy.nl/articles/Recording%20in%20Ableton%20with%20MOTU%20M2%20loopback.html</link><description>&lt;h1 id="recording-with-loopback"&gt;Recording with loopback&lt;a class="headerlink" href="#recording-with-loopback" title="Permanent link"&gt;&amp;para;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I&amp;rsquo;m able to record computer audio with my &lt;span class="caps"&gt;MOTU&lt;/span&gt; M2 in Ableton Live 11 on my&amp;nbsp;Mac!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Under preferences, set Audio Input Device to&amp;nbsp;M2&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Click the Input Config button and make sure the Stereo Inputs 1/2 and 3/4 are&amp;nbsp;highlighted&lt;/li&gt;
